  "text": ".Bundle \"h\" of 10 primary cabins and 10 secondary cabins each with 1 topdeck and 2 bottom decks with room for 11 people\ndouble cabin + top deck bottom does cabin equals ____ because\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine bread ____ people\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine bread\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine pond bread ===≈The total number of people who can be accommodated in all the cabins within the given bundle is 550. Here's the step-by-step explanation:\n\n1. Each primary cabin has 2 top decks, and each top deck can accommodate 11 people. So, each primary cabin has 2 * 11 = 22 people. Since there are 10 primary cabins, the total number of people in primary cabins is 10 * 22 = 220 people.\n\n2. Each secondary cabin has 2 bottom decks, and each bottom deck can also accommodate 11 people. So, each secondary cabin has 2 * 11 = 22 people. Since there are 10 secondary cabins, the total number of people in secondary cabins is 10 * 22 = 220 people.\n\n3. The total number of people who can be accommodated in all the cabins is the sum of the people in primary cabins and secondary cabins, which is 220 + 220 = 550 people.\n\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine bottom tid bit\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n.debugLine or\n.debugLine bottom tid bit\n.debugLine bottom tid bit\n.debugLine bottom tid bit\n.debugLine associative\n\n.debugLine dot\n\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n.debugLine hue\n\n.debugLine\n.debugLinecolor\n.debugLine\n\n.debugLine\n.debugLine\n.d